### **My recommendation for your team lead**

Don't present 7.85% as the headline result. Instead, say:

> Our baseline model achieves approximately 11% precision when targeting the highest-ranked 5% of policies, compared with a population review rate of 3.18%. This represents a 3.46-fold improvement over random targeting.

**One important qualification:** Whether 11% precision is commercially sufficient depends on engagement cost, campaign capacity and the value of a cover review. We haven't established that business threshold yet.

